#: ../developer/batches.md:16
msgid ""
"A batch request can be a chat completion (`/v1/chat/completions`), an "
"embedding (`/v1/embeddings`), an independent Responses request "
"(`/v1/responses`) or an Anthropic message. The shapes follow OpenAI's "
"Batch API and Anthropic's Message Batches API; the differences are listed"
" at the end of this page."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:22
msgid ""
"Only **internal** users and administrators can create batches unless the "
"operator opens them to other roles. A gateway with batch inference turned"
" off, or without a database, answers every batch route with `404`. "
"Otherwise every way in on this page is available: inline and file "
"batches, Anthropic Message Batches, chat, embedding and Responses "
"requests, and webhooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:29
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:31
msgid ""
"Creating a batch validates every request in it and stores them. Nothing "
"runs during that call: the batch starts as `validating`, and the "
"gateway's worker starts its requests as soon as their models have room."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:35
msgid ""
"Each request then runs exactly as if you had sent it to its endpoint "
"yourself: the same models, routing and fallback, the same price, logged "
"under your account. It counts toward your daily cost quota. It does "
"**not** use your concurrent-request limit: batch work has a separate "
"quota per role, so a running batch never blocks your own interactive "
"requests, and they never hold up the batch. Requests run in no particular"
" order, and a request that fails for a reason that may pass — a timeout, "
"a `429`, a `5xx` — is retried with backoff, up to eight attempts in all. "
"A request the model rejects (any other `4xx`) fails at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:45
msgid ""
"Before each request runs, the gateway checks the API key that created the"
" batch again:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:48
msgid ""
"if the key was revoked or has expired, or the account was suspended or "
"deleted, the batch fails;"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:50
msgid ""
"if your daily quota is used up, your batches pause until it renews at "
"midnight UTC;"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:52
msgid "if your role no longer allows batches, they pause until it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:54
msgid "So keep the key you created a batch with until the batch finishes."
msgstr ""

