#: ../developer/batches.md:297
msgid "Cancel or delete a batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:299
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`POST /v1/batches/{id}/cancel` stops a batch. Requests that have not "
"started are cancelled; running ones finish and keep their results. The "
"batch is `cancelling` until they do, then `cancelled`. Cancelling a batch"
" that has already finished returns it unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:304
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`DELETE /v1/batches/{id}` deletes a batch with its requests and results "
"and answers `{\"id\": \"batch_...\", \"object\": \"batch.deleted\", "
"\"deleted\": true}`. Its status does not matter, but deletion is blocked "
"with `409` while any request holds a live upstream lease. Cancel the "
"batch, wait for its running requests to finish (or their leases to "
"expire), then delete it. A stale `running` item whose lease has expired "
"does not block deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:311
msgid ""
"A finished batch is deleted automatically after the deployment's "
"retention period, seven days by default, so collect its results before "
"then."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:314
msgid "List your batches"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:316
msgid ""
"`GET /v1/batches` lists your own batches, newest first. `limit` is 1–100 "
"(default 20); for the next page pass `after` set to the `last_id` of the "
"previous one. The answer has the shape of a results page, with batch "
"objects in `data`. It lists OpenAI batches, inline and from files; "
"Message Batches are listed by `GET /v1/messages/batches`, and an id of "
"one API reads as not found on the other."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:323
msgid ""
"Reading, downloading, cancelling, deleting and listing your batches work "
"even if your role no longer allows creating them or your daily quota is "
"used up, so you can always collect and remove what you submitted, with "
"any of your API keys. Another user's batch reads as not found. "
"Administrators may read, cancel and delete any batch."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:329
msgid "Batches from a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:331
msgid ""
"The OpenAI flow: upload a JSONL file whose every line is one request, "
"then create a batch from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:344
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each line is `{\"custom_id\", \"method\": \"POST\", \"url\", \"body\"}`, "
"the `url` equal to the batch's `endpoint`. Every line must use the same "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:347
msgid ""
"The batch starts as `validating` while the gateway reads the file in the "
"background. If any line is invalid — not JSON, a repeated `custom_id`, "
"another `url` or model, a body the endpoint would refuse — the whole "
"batch is `failed` and nothing of it runs; `errors` lists the problems "
"with their line numbers. Otherwise it moves to `in_progress`. Once every "
"request has finished it is `finalizing` for a moment while its result "
"files are written, and then reaches its final status with "
"`output_file_id` (the successful requests) and `error_file_id` (the "
"others) set; either is `null` when it has no lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:356
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Download them with `GET /v1/files/{id}/content`. A result file is the "
"same bytes every time it is downloaded, and its size and SHA-256 (the "
"`ETag`) are fixed when the batch ends. `GET /v1/files` lists your files, "
"`GET /v1/files/{id}` returns one, and `DELETE /v1/files/{id}` deletes one"
" for good: a deleted output file is not written again, though the batch "
"still names it. Deleting an input file does not affect a batch already "
"created from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:363
msgid "The official OpenAI SDKs work with this flow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:377
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"An inline batch's results are also available as one JSONL file, in the "
"same line shape, once it has ended: `GET /v1/batches/{id}/output.jsonl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:382
msgid ""
"`/v1/messages/batches` (and `/anthropic/v1/messages/batches`) speak "
"Anthropic's Message Batches API, so the official Anthropic SDKs work "
"against it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:406
msgid ""
"Every request needs the `anthropic-version` header. `2023-06-01` and "
"`2026-10-21` are accepted; a batch keeps the version it was created with,"
" and each of its requests is checked against that version's rules (under "
"`2026-10-21`, `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are refused, as are "
"document blocks in assistant messages and citations on user text). "
"`anthropic-beta` is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:413
msgid ""
"The envelope — `custom_id` (up to 64 letters, digits, `_` and `-`, "
"unique), the number of requests, the body size — is checked at once and "
"any problem refuses the batch. Each request's `params` is then checked on"
" its own: one the gateway cannot run as written, including one naming a "
"model you may not use, becomes an `errored` result and the others still "
"run. A request is never sent with a parameter silently dropped: when a "
"model's route cannot carry a parameter (extended thinking, cache control "
"or structured output on a non-Anthropic backend, for example), the "
"request errors instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:422
msgid ""
"`request_counts` hold every request as `processing` until the whole batch"
" has `ended`; `results_url` appears then. Cancelling makes it `canceling`"
" until its running requests finish. A batch can be deleted only once it "
"has ended."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:426
msgid ""
"Each request is a single inference turn. A result that asks for a tool "
"call is for your program to carry out and send back in a new request; the"
" gateway never runs your tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:430
msgid "Embeddings and Responses in a batch"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:432
msgid ""
"`/v1/embeddings` and `/v1/responses` can be batched like chat "
"completions, inline or from a file. A batched Responses request must be "
"independent: omit `store` or set it to `false`, and leave out "
"`previous_response_id`, `conversation`, `background` and `stream`. Hosted"
" tools, file inputs and any other field the gateway would have to drop "
"are refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:438
msgid "Submitting safely twice"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:440
msgid ""
"Send an `Idempotency-Key` header with a create call (any of the three "
"APIs) to make it safe to retry. The same key with the same request "
"returns the batch the first call created, even if your quota has since "
"run out or your role changed; the same key with a different request "
"answers `409`. After the batch is deleted the key answers `410` for at "
"least a day; a key is remembered until a day after its batch ends. The "
"key belongs to your account, so any of your API keys can replay it, and a"
" replay never changes which key the batch runs under. The SDKs do not "
"send this header for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:449
msgid "Costs"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:451
msgid ""
"Every attempt at a request is recorded with what it was billed, at the "
"same point and the same price as an interactive request; a batch is never"
" billed a second time on top. `cost_usd` adds up the attempts whose cost "
"is known."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:455
msgid ""
"When an attempt's result was lost after the request had been sent — the "
"gateway timed out, or a worker stopped mid-request — the provider may "
"still have run and charged it. Its cost is then *unknown*: it is counted "
"in `cost_unknown_attempts` and left out of `cost_usd` rather than counted"
" as zero. A retried request may therefore have run more than once."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:461
msgid "Webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:463
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Instead of polling, register one HTTPS endpoint for your batches with "
"`PUT /v1/batch_webhook` (`{\"url\": \"https://…\"}`), or on the console's"
" **Batches** page. The answer carries the signing secret, `whsec_…`, "
"once; send `\"rotate_secret\": true` to get a new one. `GET "
"/v1/batch_webhook` shows the webhook, `DELETE /v1/batch_webhook` removes "
"it, and `GET /v1/batch_webhook/events` lists recent deliveries."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:470
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"When a batch ends, after its results can be read, the gateway POSTs an "
"event: `batch.completed`, `batch.failed`, `batch.expired` or "
"`batch.cancelled` for an OpenAI batch, `message_batch.ended` for a "
"Message Batch. The body names the batch only (`{\"id\", \"object\": "
"\"event\", \"type\", \"created_at\", \"data\": {\"id\"}}`); fetch the "
"results with your API key. Deliveries are signed as Standard Webhooks "
"are: verify `webhook-signature` (`v1,` and a base64 HMAC-SHA256 of "
"`\"{webhook-id}.{webhook-timestamp}.{body}\"` with the secret's base64 "
"part as the key). A delivery that is not answered with a `2xx` is retried"
" with backoff, up to eight attempts; the same event can arrive more than "
"once, so deduplicate on `webhook-id`."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:481
msgid ""
"A webhook URL must be HTTPS and reach a public address. Private, "
"loopback, link-local and cloud-metadata addresses are refused when the "
"URL is saved, again on every redirect, and again on every connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:485
msgid "Batches in the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:487
msgid ""
"The **Batches** page of the console (from the dashboard) lists your "
"batches across all three APIs with their progress, tokens and known cost,"
" and lets you cancel, delete and download results, and set up your "
"webhook."
msgstr ""

