#: ../developer/batches.md:517
msgid "Compared with OpenAI's and Anthropic's batch APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:519
msgid ""
"Batch requests cost the same as interactive ones: there is no batch "
"discount, and the gateway runs each request itself rather than handing "
"the batch to a provider's own batch service."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:522
msgid ""
"The limits are the deployment's (see [Limits](#limits)), lower than the "
"providers' own: 50,000 requests and 32 MiB per batch by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:524
msgid ""
"The 24-hour window of file batches and Message Batches is when the "
"gateway stops *starting* requests. Requests already running when it ends "
"finish, so a batch may reach its final status after `expires_at`."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:527
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The inline form, `GET /v1/batches/{id}/results`, the JSONL export, "
"`DELETE /v1/batches/{id}`, `Idempotency-Key` and the cost fields are this"
" gateway's own."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:530
msgid "Only `purpose=batch` files exist, and they serve batches only."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:531
msgid ""
"Responses requests in a batch are independent: `store: true`, "
"`previous_response_id`, `conversation`, `background` and hosted tools are"
" refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:534
msgid ""
"Message Batches belong to your account; there are no workspaces. "
"`anthropic-beta` is refused, and so are server tools, Files API sources, "
"MCP servers and containers."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:538
msgid "Running batch inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:540
msgid ""
"These settings are on the admin console's **Configuration** tab, under "
"**Batch inference**. None needs a restart: a change applies to the next "
"request and to the worker's next round."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_ENABLED`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "on"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Serve batch inference, every kind of it. Off, every batch, file and "
"webhook route answers `404` and no queued request starts; stored batches "
"are kept"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MIN_ROLE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`internal`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Lowest role that may create batches (`free`, `pro`, `internal`, `admin`)."
" A queued request also waits while its owner's role is below it"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MODEL_CONCURRENCY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "64"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Batch requests a model runs at once, across the whole deployment, when it"
" has no cap of its own. `0` pauses batch work on those models"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_YIELD_TO_INTERACTIVE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Interactive requests in flight on a model take batch slots from its cap"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_REQUESTS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "50000"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Requests one batch may hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_BODY_MB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "32"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Largest create request, in MiB"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_ACTIVE_PER_USER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "10"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Unfinished batches one user may have"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_COMPLETION_WINDOW_HOURS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "24"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Hours a new batch has before its unstarted requests expire, 1–168"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_RETENTION_DAYS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "7"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Days a finished batch and its results are kept. A batch keeps the value "
"it was created with"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_QUEUED_REQUESTS_PER_USER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "100000"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Unfinished requests one user may have across all their batches"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_ROLE_CONCURRENCY_FREE` / `_PRO` / `_INTERNAL` / `_ADMIN`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "8 / 16 / 64 / 64"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Batch requests one user of that role may have running at once, across "
"every model. Counted per gateway process (deployments run one). Separate "
"from the role's interactive concurrency limit (`user_concurrency_<role>` "
"and a user's own override apply to interactive requests only); `0` "
"removes this cap"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_SHARED_INTERACTIVE_LOAD`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Yield to the interactive requests of every gateway process, not only the "
"worker's own"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_INTERACTIVE_RESERVE`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Slots of every model's batch cap kept free for interactive requests, on "
"top of those in flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_LINE_KB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "4096"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Largest line of an input file"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_MAX_RESULT_KB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Largest response one batch request may store"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_FILES_MAX_TOTAL_MB_PER_USER`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "512"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Uploaded input files one user may keep"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_FILE_UPLOADS_PER_HOUR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "60"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Input files one user may upload per hour"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_FILE_RETENTION_DAYS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "30"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "Days an uploaded input file is kept"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_ANTHROPIC_VERSIONS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`2023-06-01,2026-10-21`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`anthropic-version` values a Message Batch may be created under"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "`BATCH_WEBHOOK_ALLOW_PRIVATE_TARGETS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid "off"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:21
msgid ""
"Let webhooks reach private and loopback addresses. For isolated test "
"deployments only"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:567
msgid ""
"`BATCH_EXPANSION_ENABLED`, which earlier versions used to hold back file "
"batches, Message Batches, embedding and Responses batches and webhooks, "
"no longer controls anything. A value left in the environment or the "
"database changes nothing, is not listed on the Configuration tab and "
"cannot be set there; the gateway keeps it, so that a rollback reads it "
"again, and warns about it once at startup. Once no earlier version will "
"run, delete the stored row (`DELETE "
"/admin/config/BATCH_EXPANSION_ENABLED`, or `python -m "
"serving.config.manage reset BATCH_EXPANSION_ENABLED`) and unset the "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:577
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A model's own cap is set in **Batch Concurrency** on the admin Settings "
"tab: empty takes `BATCH_MODEL_CONCURRENCY`, `0` pauses that model's batch"
" work, and the section shows how many batch requests each model is "
"running and how many are queued. A change reaches every gateway process "
"within about ten seconds. Behind it are `GET /admin/batch/models` and "
"`PATCH /admin/batch/models/{model_id}` with `{\"max_concurrency\": <n or "
"null>}`. The cap counts the requests of every gateway process against one"
" limit, so it does not grow with the number of processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:586
msgid ""
"Every gateway process runs a worker; requests of one batch may run in "
"several of them. A process that stops hands its unfinished requests back,"
" and the requests of one that dies are taken over by another once their "
"lease runs out, a few minutes later."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:591
msgid ""
"The batches live in the operational database: `batch_jobs`, "
"`batch_items`, `batch_attempts` (one row per attempt, with what it was "
"billed), `batch_idempotency`, `batch_files` and `batch_file_chunks`, "
"`batch_webhooks` and `batch_webhook_events`, `batch_model_limits` and a "
"few tables of scheduling state. Each request a batch runs is a row in "
"`api_logs` with `batch_job_id` set, and its item and attempt in the row's"
" metadata. Permanently deleting a user deletes their batches, files, "
"idempotency records and webhook too."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:599
msgid ""
"The admin console's **Batches** tab lists every user's batches, totals "
"them per user and lets an administrator cancel one."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:602
msgid "Upgrading a deployment"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:604
msgid ""
"A worker only runs the kinds of batch it knows: claims, expiry, "
"finalizing, validation, sealing and cleanup all skip a batch whose "
"surface, target or schema version is newer than the worker's. The workers"
" that do not know this are the old ones: a gateway older than the one "
"that added file batches and Message Batches (before #1660) has no such "
"filter and would run their requests as chat completions. New code cannot "
"change what an old process already running does, so before upgrading from"
" one of those versions, make sure no old worker is running alongside the "
"new version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:613
msgid ""
"On the old version, turn `BATCH_ENABLED` off (Configuration tab, or "
"`python -m serving.config.manage set BATCH_ENABLED false`). Within about "
"ten seconds every old process stops claiming and sweeping, and logs that "
"its batch worker is disabled. A request it was already running finishes "
"or is handed back; those are chat batches, which the new version runs "
"too."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:618
msgid ""
"Upgrade every gateway process. The new processes start with "
"`BATCH_ENABLED` still off."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:620
msgid ""
"Once no process of the old version is left (check your process manager or"
" orchestrator, not only the health endpoint), turn `BATCH_ENABLED` on."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:623
msgid ""
"Stopping every old process before any new one starts is equally safe. "
"From a version that already has file batches and Message Batches (#1660 "
"or later), a rolling upgrade needs none of this: its workers know every "
"kind."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:627
msgid "Rolling back"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:629
msgid ""
"To a version that already has file batches and Message Batches (#1660 or "
"later), roll back as usual. That version reads `BATCH_EXPANSION_ENABLED` "
"again, off by default, so new batches of the newer kinds are refused "
"until it is on; those already accepted keep running."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:634
msgid ""
"To an older version, do it while this version is still running, since "
"only it can manage the newer batches:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:637
msgid ""
"Set `BATCH_MIN_ROLE` to `admin`, so no one else can create batches. Other"
" users' queued requests then stop starting too, so their batches have to "
"be cancelled rather than waited for. To let them finish instead, skip "
"this step; step 3 still catches a batch created meanwhile."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:641
msgid ""
"Cancel (or let finish) every batch that is not an inline chat batch: the "
"admin **Batches** tab lists and cancels anyone's. A cancelled file batch "
"still needs a moment to seal. Wait until this returns no rows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:652
msgid ""
"Turn `BATCH_ENABLED` off, then run the query once more: it catches a "
"batch created between steps 2 and 3. If it returns a row, turn "
"`BATCH_ENABLED` back on and repeat step 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:655
msgid ""
"Stop every gateway process, then start the older version. It keeps "
"`BATCH_ENABLED` off; turn it on, and set `BATCH_MIN_ROLE` back, once only"
" the older version runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../developer/batches.md:659
msgid ""
"Finished batches of the newer kinds stay in the database; the older "
"version lists and purges them as if they were inline chat batches. "
"Uploaded files and webhooks stay unread until the next upgrade. Turning "
"`BATCH_ENABLED` off is not enough on its own: it stops the newer "
"version's worker too, so the newer batches would never drain."
msgstr ""

